<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 92,644 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 92,644 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 92,644 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 75,573 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	Dec 29</p>
<p>    Export cargo		28,776	22,328</p>
<p>    Import cargo		63,868	53,245</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     30,099	 Eramus		 31/12</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     34,500	 Lucky Fortune	31/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Courage    01/01</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,406	 Asku		   01/01</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
